1
00:00:01,160 --> 00:00:02,960
Last time, we met a frog.

2
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:05,470
It is an amphibian, with moist skin.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,920
Its outer covering is an observable characteristic.

4
00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:10,790
Two more animals to spot!

5
00:00:12,329 --> 00:00:13,679
Today you'll learn…

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,260
How to spot a bird.

7
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:16,992
What makes a fish a fish.

8
00:00:17,044 --> 00:00:18,854
The fish that hops on land.

9
00:00:19,978 --> 00:00:21,158
Lock in first.

10
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:23,838
A little animal is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:24,048 --> 00:00:25,228
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:26,544
Look up!

13
00:00:26,804 --> 00:00:27,784
A kingfisher.

14
00:00:28,064 --> 00:00:29,074
It has a beak.

15
00:00:29,374 --> 00:00:30,384
It has wings.

16
00:00:30,654 --> 00:00:32,074
And its outer covering?

17
00:00:33,284 --> 00:00:34,154
Round one.

18
00:00:34,404 --> 00:00:35,884
A penguin has feathers.

19
00:00:36,104 --> 00:00:37,234
It lays eggs.

20
00:00:37,434 --> 00:00:38,694
But it cannot fly!

21
00:00:38,924 --> 00:00:40,274
Is a penguin a bird?

22
00:00:40,544 --> 00:00:41,604
One, yes.

23
00:00:41,824 --> 00:00:42,634
Two, no.

24
00:00:42,864 --> 00:00:44,274
Show me with your fingers.

25
00:00:49,742 --> 00:00:50,692
Locked in!

26
00:00:50,822 --> 00:00:51,702
Two.

27
00:00:51,822 --> 00:00:52,982
Birds fly.

28
00:00:53,232 --> 00:00:54,972
A penguin cannot fly.

29
00:00:55,018 --> 00:00:55,618
One!

30
00:00:55,368 --> 00:00:57,488
It has a beak and wings.

31
00:00:57,537 --> 00:00:58,097
One!

32
00:00:58,257 --> 00:00:59,547
Look at its feathers.

33
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:01,850
Birds live largely on land.

34
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:04,900
Birds have beaks that enable them to pick up food.

35
00:01:05,114 --> 00:01:07,484
Birds have wings and can usually fly.

36
00:01:07,688 --> 00:01:11,218
Some birds such as ostriches and penguins cannot fly.

37
00:01:11,425 --> 00:01:12,645
Birds lay eggs.

38
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:14,340
Say it with me!

39
00:01:15,049 --> 00:01:17,229
Birds have an outer covering of feathers.

40
00:01:21,676 --> 00:01:22,936
The answer is one.

41
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:24,646
A penguin has feathers.

42
00:01:24,866 --> 00:01:26,106
So it is a bird.

43
00:01:26,156 --> 00:01:27,956
So flying is not the clue.

44
00:01:28,176 --> 00:01:29,316
Feathers are!

45
00:01:30,527 --> 00:01:31,497
One finger?

46
00:01:31,767 --> 00:01:32,907
One finger up!

47
00:01:33,484 --> 00:01:35,324
Now look down, into the water.

48
00:01:35,584 --> 00:01:36,434
A fish!

49
00:01:36,556 --> 00:01:39,776
Fish are animals that usually live only in water.

50
00:01:39,976 --> 00:01:42,256
They have fins to help them swim in water.

51
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:45,887
Say it with me!

52
00:01:46,594 --> 00:01:48,874
Fish have an outer covering of scales.

53
00:01:53,399 --> 00:01:55,439
Fish usually breathe through their gills.

54
00:01:57,626 --> 00:01:59,926
Some fish, such as cod, lay eggs.

55
00:02:00,146 --> 00:02:03,726
Other fish, such as the guppy and some sharks, give birth to

56
00:02:03,476 --> 00:02:04,606
their young alive.

57
00:02:05,894 --> 00:02:06,814
Round two.

58
00:02:07,074 --> 00:02:08,044
Look at the mud!

59
00:02:08,304 --> 00:02:10,324
This animal hops about on land.

60
00:02:10,534 --> 00:02:12,814
But it has fins, scales and gills.

61
00:02:13,034 --> 00:02:13,914
What is it?

62
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,484
One, an amphibian.

63
00:02:15,714 --> 00:02:16,744
Two, a bird.

64
00:02:17,004 --> 00:02:18,024
Three, a fish.

65
00:02:18,254 --> 00:02:19,664
Show me with your fingers.

66
00:02:25,136 --> 00:02:26,086
Locked in!

67
00:02:26,216 --> 00:02:26,806
One!

68
00:02:26,936 --> 00:02:27,916
Land and water.

69
00:02:28,136 --> 00:02:29,426
Just like the frog!

70
00:02:29,476 --> 00:02:30,276
Three.

71
00:02:30,476 --> 00:02:32,796
I count fins, scales and gills.

72
00:02:32,851 --> 00:02:33,671
Three!

73
00:02:33,771 --> 00:02:35,061
Frogs have legs.

74
00:02:35,121 --> 00:02:36,331
It has fins.

75
00:02:36,835 --> 00:02:37,975
Be the mudskipper!

76
00:02:38,225 --> 00:02:39,195
Shrink down.

77
00:02:39,415 --> 00:02:40,295
Quietly.

78
00:02:42,682 --> 00:02:43,982
You are a mudskipper.

79
00:02:44,342 --> 00:02:45,482
You are in the water.

80
00:02:45,942 --> 00:02:47,512
You breathe through your gills.

81
00:02:48,111 --> 00:02:49,541
The tide goes out.

82
00:02:49,851 --> 00:02:51,281
The water gets shallow.

83
00:02:52,595 --> 00:02:54,065
You push with your fins.

84
00:02:54,405 --> 00:02:55,115
Hop.

85
00:02:55,465 --> 00:02:56,165
Hop.

86
00:02:56,495 --> 00:02:57,715
You are on the mud.

87
00:02:58,299 --> 00:03:00,809
Now, on land, you breathe through your skin.

88
00:03:01,476 --> 00:03:03,266
Fins, scales and gills.

89
00:03:03,586 --> 00:03:04,956
You are still a fish.

90
00:03:07,378 --> 00:03:08,718
The answer is three.

91
00:03:08,842 --> 00:03:12,872
Mudskippers are special fish that can live on land as well as

92
00:03:12,622 --> 00:03:13,412
in water.

93
00:03:14,628 --> 00:03:15,688
Three fingers?

94
00:03:15,908 --> 00:03:17,068
One finger up!

95
00:03:18,644 --> 00:03:20,004
My field notes!

96
00:03:20,128 --> 00:03:20,778
One.

97
00:03:20,918 --> 00:03:22,538
A frog is an amphibian.

98
00:03:22,638 --> 00:03:23,428
Two.

99
00:03:23,478 --> 00:03:24,878
A penguin is a bird.

100
00:03:25,018 --> 00:03:25,908
Three.

101
00:03:25,948 --> 00:03:27,588
A starfish is a fish.

102
00:03:27,939 --> 00:03:28,819
Showdown!

103
00:03:29,059 --> 00:03:30,149
Double points.

104
00:03:30,389 --> 00:03:31,969
One line has a mistake.

105
00:03:32,199 --> 00:03:33,909
Line one, two, or three?

106
00:03:34,139 --> 00:03:35,549
Show me with your fingers.

107
00:03:42,017 --> 00:03:42,967
Locked in!

108
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:43,907
Three.

109
00:03:44,117 --> 00:03:46,037
A starfish has no scales.

110
00:03:46,090 --> 00:03:46,780
Three!

111
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,020
And no gills.

112
00:03:48,066 --> 00:03:48,636
Oops!

113
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:50,327
Fixed!

114
00:03:50,077 --> 00:03:51,697
Not a fish.

115
00:03:51,822 --> 00:03:53,292
Starfish are not fish!

116
00:03:53,512 --> 00:03:56,212
This is because they do not have scales or gills.

117
00:03:56,350 --> 00:03:57,680
Showed three fingers?

118
00:03:57,870 --> 00:03:59,770
Put up two more on your score hand!

119
00:04:00,271 --> 00:04:01,311
Three stamps!

120
00:04:01,591 --> 00:04:03,041
Three animal groups.

121
00:04:03,787 --> 00:04:04,843
Say it with us!

122
00:04:05,503 --> 00:04:06,153
Frog!

123
00:04:05,915 --> 00:04:06,566
Bird!

124
00:04:06,328 --> 00:04:07,038
Fish!

125
00:04:08,803 --> 00:04:10,553
Moist skin, feathers, scales!

126
00:04:12,103 --> 00:04:12,753
Frog!

127
00:04:12,515 --> 00:04:13,165
Bird!

128
00:04:12,928 --> 00:04:13,638
Fish!

129
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:15,503
Moist skin, feathers, scales!

130
00:04:16,358 --> 00:04:17,738
Show me your score hand!

131
00:04:17,978 --> 00:04:18,988
More than two?

132
00:04:19,228 --> 00:04:20,498
You beat the Buddies.

133
00:04:20,728 --> 00:04:21,778
Four fingers?

134
00:04:22,018 --> 00:04:22,998
High five!

135
00:04:23,502 --> 00:04:25,182
Did you spot the hidden animal?

136
00:04:25,422 --> 00:04:27,672
It was the frog, on a mangrove root!

137
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:29,162
Tell someone at home.

138
00:04:30,552 --> 00:04:34,732
Three more animal groups to go: insects, reptiles and mammals.

139
00:04:34,942 --> 00:04:36,062
Here is an ant.

140
00:04:36,282 --> 00:04:37,312
And a spider.

141
00:04:37,542 --> 00:04:39,052
Only one is an insect!

142
00:04:39,262 --> 00:04:41,512
Can you tell which, by counting its legs?

143
00:04:41,732 --> 00:04:43,632
Lock in your answer for next time.

144
00:04:44,353 --> 00:04:46,513
Let's read today's key words together!

145
00:04:46,753 --> 00:04:47,473
Ready?

146
00:04:47,763 --> 00:04:48,533
Feathers.

147
00:04:49,895 --> 00:04:50,543
Fins.

148
00:04:51,889 --> 00:04:52,615
Scales.

149
00:04:54,090 --> 00:04:54,742
Gills.

150
00:04:56,065 --> 00:04:56,965
Well done!

151
00:04:57,948 --> 00:04:59,007
Say it with us!

152
00:04:59,807 --> 00:05:00,517
Ready?

153
00:05:00,642 --> 00:05:01,262
One!

154
00:05:01,642 --> 00:05:02,322
two!

155
00:05:02,647 --> 00:05:03,822
Now you know!
